  <ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock id="Tag3505" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="Tag3506" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock id="Tag3507" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantLeaseholdsThatHaveBeenAcquiredOrGivenAssignedOrSurrenderedTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="Tag3508" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Effective January 1, 2025, Eolian, L.P., Oklahoma Office of the Attorney, and The Petroleum Alliance of Oklahoma all became non-transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;Effective February 1, 2025, &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;ExxonMobil&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt; Power and Gas Services Inc. became a non-transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;Effective March 1, 2025, Advanced Energy United, Inc. became a non-transmission owning member.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;Effective April 1, 2025, &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Poudre&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt; Valley Rural Electric Association, Inc. became a non-transmission owning member.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;Effective May 1, 2025, Oxy USA Inc. and Hannon Armstrong Capital, LLC became non-transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;Effective June 1, 2025, ONE Gas, Inc. became a non-transmission owning member.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;Effective July 1, 2025, &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Conoco&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt; Phillips Company, Matador Production Company and &lt;/font&gt;Targa&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt; Northern Delaware LLC became non-transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Effective August 1, 2025, GridLiance Peaks LLC, Validus Energy and Voltus, Inc. became non-transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Effective September 1, 2025, Networked Transmission Systems, Inc. became a non-transmission owning member.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;Effective October 1, 2025, NGL Water Solutions, LLC and Upper Missouri G. &amp;amp; T. Electric Cooperative, Inc. became non-transmission owning members.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="Tag3509" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;In 2025, Southwest Power Pool (SPP) established a new $150,000,000 revolving line of credit with a commercial bank expiring in 2033 &lt;em&gt;(Docket number ES25-33)&lt;/em&gt;. At December 31, 2025, $14,600,000 was borrowed against this line. The agreement has a variable interest rate based on the Daily Simple Secured Overnight Funding Rate (SOFR) index plus a credit margin that varies according to cash collateral provided to secure the loan. The margin applicable at December 31, 2025, was 2.80% resulting in an effective rate of 6.67%. The Company&amp;#8217;s line of credit requires compliance with certain financial and non-financial covenants as well as periodic reporting requirements. &lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"&gt;SPP &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;has a $30,000,000 revolving line of credit with a commercial bank&amp;#160;expiring in 2027 &lt;em&gt;(Docket number ES25-51)&lt;/em&gt;. At December 31, 2025, no amounts were borrowed against this line. The agreement has a variable interest rate based on the Daily Simple Secured Overnight Funding Rate (SOFR) index plus a 1.1% credit margin. The Company&amp;#8217;s line of credit requires compliance with certain financial and non-financial covenants as well as periodic reporting requirements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-autospace: none;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black;"&gt;SPP &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif;"&gt;has an $80,000,000 revolving commitment from another commercial bank expiring in 2027 that could be utilized for both revolving and term loans &lt;em&gt;(Docket number ES22-33)&lt;/em&gt;. At December 31, 2025, $39,670,000 was outstanding against the revolving balance and $18,997,254 was the outstanding term loan balance. The agreement has a revolving interest rate based on the Secured Overnight Funding Rate (SOFR) index plus a 1.5% credit margin, with a floor of 2.50%. The Company&amp;#8217;s line of credit requires compliance with certain financial and non-financial covenants as well as periodic reporting requirements.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock id="Tag3510" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInArticlesOfIncorporationOrAmendmentsToCharterTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock id="Tag3511" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfEstimatedAnnualEffectAndNatureOfAnyImportantWageScaleChangesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="Tag3512" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock id="Tag3513" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfMateriallyImportantTransactionsOfTheRespondentNotDisclosedElsewhereTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock id="Tag3514" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;N/A&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantChangesRelatedToRespondentCompanyAppearingInAnnualReportToStockholdersTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="Tag3515" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;"&gt;Effective January 2, 2025, Michael Desselle, Vice President and Chief Compliance and Administrative Officer retired.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Effective February 3, 2025, Sam Ellis, Vice President of Information Technology retired.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;"&gt;Effective March 3, 2025, Felek Abbas was named as the new Senior Vice President and Chief Technology and Security Officer. The new position combines Felek&amp;#8217;s previous duties as Vice President and Chief Security Officer with new responsibilities of overseeing information technology and corporate facilities.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;The Southwest Power Pool (SPP) board of directors selected L&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;anny &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Nickell&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt; to&lt;/font&gt; serve as the new President and Chief Executive Officer effective April 1, 2025. Lanny was &lt;/font&gt;SPP&amp;#8217;s&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 12pt;"&gt; Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer. Lanny replaces Barbara &lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Sugg&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: 'times new roman', times;"&gt;,&lt;/font&gt; who announced her April 2025 retirement in December 2024.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;"&gt;Effective April 1, 2025, Antoine Lucas was named Executive Vice President and Chief Operating Officer. Prior to this role, Antoine was Vice President of Markets.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;"&gt;Effective April 1, 2025, Carrie Simpson was named Vice President of Markets.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;"&gt;Effective April 1, 2025, Kevin Bryant, was named Executive Vice President of Stakeholder Affairs and Chief Strategy Officer.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;"&gt;Effective August 12, 2025, the Southwest Power Pool (SPP) board of directors announced Raymond Hepper assumed the role of board chair.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;"&gt;Effective October 1, 2025, CJ Brown was named Vice President of Operations. CJ will replace Bruce Rew, the current Senior Vice President of Operations, who announced his upcoming retirement. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="mso-margin-top-alt: auto; margin-bottom: 14.0pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: 'Times New Roman',serif; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;"&gt;Effective October 13, 2025, the Southwest Power Pool (SPP) board of directors announced Stuart Solomon assumed the role of board vice chair.&lt;font style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="Tag3516" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
