&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company has estimated the long-term rate of return on plan assets based primarily on historical returns on plan assets, adjusted for changes in target portfolio allocations and recent changes in long-term interest rates based on publicly available information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;For measurement purposes, a trend rate of 6.5% was assumed in 2025 for the increase in per capita cost of covered healthcare benefits for those aged pre-65, decreasing gradually to 5.0% by the year 2030 and continuing to decrease slowly thereafter. For 2025, no health cost trend assumption is applied for post-65 since those contributions are a fixed amount. For 2024, a trend rate of 6.1% for those aged pre-65 and 6.5% for those aged post-65 annual rate of increase in the per capita cost of covered healthcare benefits in the next year was assumed with the rate decreasing gradually to 4.80% pre-65 and 5.00% post-65 by the year 2029 and continuing to decrease slowly thereafter&lt;/p&gt;
