&lt;div class="Section_5"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt; -aw-outline-level: 2;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt; -aw-outline-level: 2;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; text-align: justify; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 11pt; -aw-outline-level: 2;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold; font-style: italic;"&gt;Defined Contribution and Deferred Compensation Plans&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company has a 401(k) defined contribution plan covering substantially all employees. The Company matches contributions at 4.75% for those employees deferring 6% of compensation, with the match fluctuating from 1% to 4.75% for each percentage of compensation contributed under 6%. Contributions to the plan were $5,147 and $4,697 for 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;The Company has a 457(b) nonqualified tax-deferred compensation plan. This plan is an unfunded plan maintained for the purpose of providing deferred compensation for a select group of management or highly compensated employees and, therefore, is intended to be exempt from the participation, vesting, funding and fiduciary requirements of Title I of the &lt;font style="font-style: italic;"&gt;Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974&lt;/font&gt; (ERISA). Accumulated contributions and earnings of $6,539 and $6,143 are recorded in other long-term liabilities at December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively. The Company also offers a 457(f) nonqualified tax-deferred compensation plan to a select group of executive management. The 457(f) plan was intended to be exempt from the participation, vesting, funding and fiduciary requirements of Title I of ERISA and serves to further supplement benefits lost due to IRS limits on compensation and benefits. There were accrued benefits of $280 recorded in current liabilities at December 31, 2025 and $1,908 recorded in other long-term liabilities at December 31, 2024 for the 457(f) plan participants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;Beginning January 1, 2024, the Company provides a long-term incentive plan for certain members of executive management. The plan provides for the payment of incentive-based cash compensation based on performance measures of the Company over a rolling three-year period.&amp;#160; The estimated liability from the plan at December 31, 2025 and 2024 was $1,293 and $286, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 18pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-indent: -18pt; page-break-inside: avoid; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt; -aw-import: list-item; -aw-list-level-number: 0; -aw-list-number-format: 'Note %0.'; -aw-list-number-styles: 'decimal'; -aw-list-number-values: '7'; -aw-list-padding-sml: 13.99pt; -aw-outline-level: 1;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Note 7.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="width: 13.99pt; font: 7pt 'Times New Roman'; display: inline-block; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Revenue from Contracts with Customers&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt; text-align: justify;"&gt;In 2025 and 2024, the Company&amp;#8217;s revenues were derived from a number of sources including tariff administration fees, FERC fees, engineering studies, contract services, and other miscellaneous income sources. The table below presents a complete breakdown of the Company&amp;#8217;s revenues:&lt;/p&gt;
